invariant: INV-5
file: pem_files.c
catches: pem_files_test
reason: ch_p256_key_from_pem stops comparing the key with the end-entity
  certificate, so a key file paired with the wrong chain decodes, and
  every client refuses the server's CertificateVerify instead of the
  operator seeing CH_EINVAL at provisioning. test_key_refusals passes the
  intermediate's certificate and a bare point as the leaf.

--- old
             (file_point == NULL || ct_memeq(file_point, pub, 64) != 0) &&
             leaf_holds(leaf, leaf_len, pub);
--- new
             (file_point == NULL || ct_memeq(file_point, pub, 64) != 0);
    (void)leaf_holds;
